    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "story",
        "type": "story",
        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "Big and small numbers"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "The distance to the Sun is about 150 000 000 km and a virus may be 0.0000001 m wide. Scientists write such numbers compactly. And roots like root 2 need careful handling too."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "surd",
          "surd laws",
          "like surds",
          "simplify",
          "rationalise",
          "conjugate",
          "a x 10^n"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "A surd is an irrational root such as root 2, root 3 or the cube root of 5.\nLaws: root a x root b = root (ab) and root a / root b = root (a/b).\nLike surds can be added: 3 root 2 + 5 root 2 = 8 root 2.\nSimplify surds by taking out square factors: root 18 = root 9 x root 2 = 3 root 2.\nTo rationalise 1/(root a) multiply the top and bottom by root a, giving root a / a.\nFor 1/(a + root b) multiply by the conjugate (a - root b) to use (a + root b)(a - root b) = a squared - b.\nScientific notation writes a number as a x 10^n with 1 less than or equal to a less than 10 and n an integer."
        }
      },
      {
